    "question": "On Thursday Walmart sold 210 pounds of ground beef. On Friday they sold twice that amount. On Saturday they only sold 150 pounds.  What was the average amount of beef sold per day?",
    "gold": "260",
    "answer": "On Friday Walmart sold 2 * 210 pounds = <<2*210=420>>420 pounds.\nFor all three days Walmart sold 210 + 420 + 150 pounds = <<210+420+150=780>>780 pounds.\nThe average amount of beef sold per day is 780 pounds / 3 days = <<780/3=260>>260 pounds.\n#### 260"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To find the average amount of beef sold per day, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine the amount of beef sold on each day.\n2. Sum the amounts sold over the three days.\n3. Divide the total amount by the number of days to find the average.\n\nFirst, let's find the amount of beef sold on each day:\n- On Thursday, Walmart sold 210 pounds of ground beef.\n- On Friday, they sold twice the amount sold on Thursday, which is \\(2 \\times 210 = 420\\) pounds.\n- On Saturday, they sold 150 pounds of ground beef.\n\nNext, we sum the amounts sold over the three days:\n\\[210 + 420 + 150 = 780\\]\n\nNow, we divide the total amount by the number of days (which is 3) to find the average:\n\\[\\frac{780}{3} = 260\\]\n\nTherefore, the average amount of beef sold per day is \\(\\boxed{260}\\).",
